  No full intel_crtc_min_cdclk, plane bandwidth/audio policy, PCODE or clock writes.

Optional upstream_clock/upstream_readout tests extract and compile local MIT
C bodies and headers at runtime. They do not distribute a Linux C copy or
implement a kernel LinuxKPI layer. Temporary oracle files are removed.

The excerpt inventory scanner also finds one normalized textual C-code match
at both thresholds25/40 in tests/upstream_clock.rs: the conventional sizeof
ARRAY_SIZE expression used by the original host compile shim. This is not an
imported C driver or a quoted Linux prose block. Accounted as one outside-fence
code line in the repository's scanner baseline; no fenced quote or range marker.

src/dkl_phy.rs:
  drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_dkl_phy.c:
  dkl_phy_set_hip_idx, intel_dkl_phy_{read,write,rmw,posting_read}
  intel_dkl_phy_regs.h: four ADL-P TC apertures/bank/index layout
  Copyright © 2022 Intel Corporation.
src/dpll_mgr.rs additionally includes dkl_pll_get_hw_state, ADL-P
  intel_tc_pll_enable_reg routing and its display_regs.h register fields.
  Copyright © 2006-2016 / 2025 Intel Corporation.
  Power and global HIP locking are explicit backend lifetime contracts.
  Readout restores and verifies firmware's selector under a single lock;
  i915 driver-owned individual access routines retain their original sequence.
  dco_khz is derived metadata, excluded from raw state comparisons.

src/universal_plane.rs:
